    {
      "stem": "Why is RAG needed when Large Language Models already contain knowledge from training, and how does it address limitations such as outdated information, hallucinations, and the inability to access private or frequently changing data?",
      "tag": "Fresh evidence and private data",
      "answer": "c",
      "options": [
        "It permanently prevents hallucinations by allowing only words copied from model training.",
        "It makes previously learned model knowledge unnecessary for understanding any user request.",
        "It supplies current or restricted evidence when pretrained knowledge is insufficient.",
        "It guarantees every retrieved document is accurate, authorized, and recently updated."
      ],
