      "explanation": "<strong>In simple words:</strong> In Python, load a PDF, split its text, store searchable vectors, retrieve matching passages, then let an LLM answer using them.",
      "figure": "<div class=\"rag-fig rag-illustrated rag-layer5\" data-scene=\"python-pdf-faiss-retrieval\"><span class=\"rag-kicker\">5 / VISUAL LESSON</span><h3>PDF-powered Python RAG</h3><div class=\"rag-scroll\"><svg class=\"rag-new-diagram-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 240\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A PDF is parsed into chunks, converted into embedding vectors, indexed in FAISS and retrieved for the LLM\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"898\" height=\"238\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fcfeff\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><rect x=\"35\" y=\"91\" width=\"51\" height=\"67\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><text x=\"45\" y=\"115\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#345a73\">DOC</text><line x1=\"44\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"76\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#95b1b9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"44\" y1=\"133\" x2=\"76\" y2=\"133\" stroke=\"#95b1b9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"44\" y1=\"142\" x2=\"76\" y2=\"142\" stroke=\"#95b1b9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"187\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#345a73\">PDF</text><path d=\"M100 121 L164 121 m-9 -6 l9 6 -9 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#608ca5\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"172\" y=\"69\" width=\"140\" height=\"97\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#eaf6ff\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><text x=\"186\" y=\"109\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#345a73\">TEXT CHUNKS</text><path d=\"M317 121 L373 121 m-9 -6 l9 6 -9 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#608ca5\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"380\" y=\"69\" width=\"143\" height=\"97\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#eaf9ef\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><text x=\"393\" y=\"109\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#345a73\">EMBEDDINGS</text><rect x=\"393\" y=\"124\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#83bfac\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><rect x=\"413\" y=\"124\" width=\"12\" height=\"17\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#83bfac\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><rect x=\"433\" y=\"124\" width=\"12\" height=\"22\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#83bfac\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><rect x=\"453\" y=\"124\" width=\"12\" height=\"27\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#83bfac\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><rect x=\"473\" y=\"124\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#83bfac\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><rect x=\"493\" y=\"124\" width=\"12\" height=\"20\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#83bfac\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><path d=\"M527 121 L582 121 m-9 -6 l9 6 -9 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#608ca5\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"589\" y=\"69\" width=\"130\" height=\"97\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#f1effc\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"109\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#345a73\">FAISS</text><text x=\"607\" y=\"137\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#345a73\">top-K index</text><path d=\"M724 121 L769 121 m-9 -6 l9 6 -9 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#608ca5\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"777\" y=\"69\" width=\"100\" height=\"97\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff0df\" stroke=\"#a3c7ce\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><text x=\"801\" y=\"114\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#345a73\">LLM</text><text x=\"797\" y=\"141\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#345a73\">answer</text></svg></div><div class=\"rag-python\"><div class=\"rag-python-head\">rag_app.py — example with pypdf, sentence-transformers, faiss-cpu, openai</div><pre><code>from pypdf import PdfReader\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nimport faiss\nfrom openai import OpenAI\n\ntext = \"\\n\".join(p.extract_text() or \"\" for p in PdfReader(\"handbook.pdf\").pages)\nchunks = [text[i:i+700] for i in range(0, len(text), 600)]\nencoder = SentenceTransformer(\"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")\nvectors = encoder.encode(chunks, normalize_embeddings=True).astype(\"float32\")\nindex = faiss.IndexFlatIP(vectors.shape[1])\nindex.add(vectors)\nquery = \"What changed in the policy?\"\nq = encoder.encode([query], normalize_embeddings=True).astype(\"float32\")\nscores, ids = index.search(q, min(3, len(chunks)))\ncontext = \"\\n\\n\".join(chunks[i] for i in ids[0])\nprompt = f\"Answer using this evidence:\\n{context}\\n\\nQuestion: {query}\"\nreply = OpenAI().responses.create(model=\"gpt-4.1-mini\", input=prompt)\nprint(reply.output_text)</code></pre></div><p class=\"rag-caption\">PDF → extracted text → overlapping chunks → embedding vectors → FAISS → prompt → LLM. Scanned PDFs may require OCR.</p></div>",
      "technicalExplanation": "<strong>Correct: A.</strong> A complete Python RAG application can read PDF text, split it into overlapping chunks, encode chunks with an embedding model, store vectors in FAISS or Chroma, retrieve top matches and prompt an LLM with those passages. Scanned PDF pages require OCR."
    },
